  (219, 'How slice 4.3 is built (`slice-4-3.md`), from G15 and G20. The checker is a built-in job: each wake lists the repository''s open pull requests with the API''s checks token, takes one head commit not yet reviewed, writes a review with one call to Claude Opus 5.5 at medium effort (no tools, no session) from the pull request, its diff (60,000 characters at most), the change''s brief and the decisions near it, and posts it as a comment review with `GITHUB_REVIEW_TOKEN`, which can only comment. Pull requests from forks and drafts are not reviewed. Each head is reviewed once; a failed post is tried twice more. A pull request that belongs to a change gets one line in its thread. The production check after merge (157) is left for a later job', 'Reading open pull requests on reconcile needs no new route (G15). A review with no tools can at worst say something wrong in a comment, so text in a pull request cannot make it do more; leaving out forks keeps text anyone on GitHub can write out of the bot''s own posts, as 181 and 189 do for the teammate', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-26T00:00:00Z', 'import', '219')
